The Witcher 3 wild Hunt is still getting  new updates and CD projekt Red has  detailed what to expect when the next  major update arrives on December 14th  one of the big new features being added  is a photo mode which will let players  take photos and share them there will be  a photo mode contest to come later on  the studio set additionally there is a  new camera mode coming that moves the  camera closer to geralt players can mix  and match the camera setup for different  situations like exploring combat and  riding Roach The Witcher 3 is also  adding Ray tracing and ambient occlusion  on PC as well as an Ultra Plus setting  that introduces more details on  background characters and environmental  elements for PlayStation 5 and Xbox  series X and S players can look forward  to Performance and quality modes  additionally PS5 and Xbox series X  players will get ray tracing ambient  occlusion and other graphical features  these won't come to the less powerful  Series S but that system does have have  30 FPS and 60 FPS options to choose from  on PS5 The Witcher 3 will use the Dual  sense controller's haptic feedback and  adaptive triggers so players will feel  the action when they smack an enemy with  a sword or perform Magic on consoles  there will also be a new special mode  where players can hold down the left  trigger and use face buttons to cast  signs instead of needing to access the  radial menu each time there are a  variety of other quality of life  improvements coming with the update  including new walking and jogging  options for geralt and the ability to  change the size of the game's subtitles  cutscenes should be improved too to  address stuttering issues that could  appear additionally players can pause  the game's cutscenes with a new update  the full patch notes will be shared  closer to launch the developers said  teasing that there will be additional  surprises to come content inspired by  Netflix's which a TV show is also coming  to The Witcher 3 including swords based  on what Henry Cavill wielded during  season 1 and 2 what's more cross  progression is coming to The Witcher 3  so players can switch between platforms  more easily going forward  as for why CD projekt Red is continuing  to support The Witcher 3 in this way the  game has sold an astonishing 40 million  plus copies and it continues to be  popular thanks in part to the Netflix TV  series a fourth which a game is now in  development in addition to a remake of  the original Witcher the new update  arrives on December 14th alongside the  complete edition which includes the base  game all DLC and the two major  expansions hearts of stone and blood and  wine at launch the complete edition will  be digital only but a physical version  is coming later for anyone who already  owns The Witcher 3 wild Hunt on PS4 Xbox  One and PC they can get the next gen  upgrades for free what upgrades are you  looking forward to the most in the Next  Gen update for The Witcher 3 let us know  in the comments and we'll see you next  time on Gamespot news  foreign
 

